<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were steady to higher on Friday in anticipation of higher interest rates at the treasury bills auction on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>The one week to one month rates rose, while the rest were steady.</p>
<p>&quot;Interest rates are slowly creeping up. That's the banks' view,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Central Bank has been giving signals. It wants rates to go up a bit,&quot; she said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  APRIL 18		 APRIL 17</p>
<p>    1 W		9  3/4		  9 11/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  3/4		  9 11/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9  7/8		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9 15/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10			9 15/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/4		 10  1/4</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/2		 10  1/2</p>
<p>    VAL		18-Apr		  17-Apr</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
